id.instance: String (TS "c<n>")
num.game: i32
num.cursor: u32
map.ordered: IndexMap
bag.data: IndexMap<String, serde_json::Value>
error.style: Result<_, StoreError> in the store (StoreError::Other(TS message), StoreError::Duplicate { match_id }); anyhow::Result in migrate and the CLIs, with TS's messages
null.optional: Option + skip_serializing_if
null.nullable: Option, serialised null
case.json: camelCase via serde rename_all
case.rust: snake_case
state.mut: &mut GameState writes, &GameState reads, &mut EngineSink for TS sink mutators (not used in this chunk)
rng.source: Rng::new(&state.seed, state.rng_cursor) and write the cursor back (not used in this chunk)
hook.style: Arc<dyn Fn + Send + Sync> via hook(); no fn pointers, no Box (the fake's clock, on_call and redemption hooks are Arc<dyn Fn + Send + Sync> too)
registry.style: OnceLock set once by register_all; fused scripts built on lookup from state (not used in this chunk)
async.style: tokio in crates/server only; none in pure crates; the fake's store fns are sync, only fake::begin awaits the lock
log.style: tracing JSON to stdout, server only
store.fake: one FakeData behind Arc<tokio::sync::Mutex>; FakeTx = guard + snapshot, restored on drop without commit
store.ints: epoch ms and counts i64, ratings f64, quantities i32, caps usize
store.tuples: TS tuples are Rust tuples (players.0, sides.0, TrioSlots 3-tuple)
migrate.checksum: jackioh_engine::replay::fnv1a32_utf16 over include_str! text
